  m_Name: Scene07EvidenceQuestion
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::AdaptiveOhmsLaw.QuestionDefinition
  questionId: S07_EvidenceConclusion
  concepts: 060000000000000001000000
  questionText: With the resistance kept the same, what happened to the current as
    the voltage increased?
  answers:
  - The current increased.
  - The current decreased.
  - The current stayed the same.
  correctAnswer: 0
  difficulty: 1
  hints:
  - Look at your observation table. Compare the current at 1 V with the current at
    3 V.
  - At 1 V, current was 0.20 A. At 3 V, current was 0.60 A. 0.60 A is larger than
    0.20 A.
  - With resistance held constant, higher voltage provides more electrical push,
    increasing current.
  masteryImpact: 1
